17] [17592186165722 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537645 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165722 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165722 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165722 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186537609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165722 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e609e883-1558-50e2-a2ac-f01133148f75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186537592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186537531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186165734 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "47e4c0ba-9e7f-5fb9-9608-805ed6d49159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166640 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8440" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166640 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle \\int 4\\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166640 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41c8053f-0ad2-5b59-ba77-8f4fda1db022" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166640 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin {2\\theta}=2\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the double-angle formula for the hyperbolic sine:\n\n$$\n\\sinh {2\\theta} =2\\sinh \\theta \\cosh \\theta\n$$\n\n \n\nLetting $\\theta= 2x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\sinh {4x} =2\\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sinh {4x}= \\sinh 2x \\cosh 2x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166641 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8441" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166641 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\cosh^2{x} + \\sinh^2{x}\\ \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166641 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b6c11fbd-00db-5506-baf0-2b6a94bfa6e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166641 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\cos{2x}= \\cos^2{x}-\\sin^2{x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh 2x = \\cosh^2{x} + \\sinh^2{x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166642 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166642 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 2\\cosh^2 x \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166642 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c91d7451-c9b5-57a1-9284-ec3fb617220c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166642 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\cos{2x} =2\\cos^2 x -1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh{2x} =2\\cosh^2 x -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n\\cosh^2 x = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\left(\\cosh 2x +1 \\right).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{cosh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166643 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8443" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166643 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\ln 2} 8\\sinh^2{x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166643 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d3a47d6-5a07-5fb6-9f57-23e74a7ba24f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166643 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\cos {2x}=1-2\\sin^2x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cosh{2x} = 1+ 2\\sinh^2{x}\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n\\sinh^2x = \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\cosh {2x} -1\\right ).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}8{sinh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x-4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x-4x)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-(2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =({2}^{2}-{2}^{-2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166802 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166802 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166802 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167416 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166802 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166802 