#edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167416 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate\n$\\int 6\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167416 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b665dec3-ff7b-5e09-a4a1-c211a5998c94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167416 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the double-angle formula for the hyperbolic sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 6\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95873" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\int (3{cosh}^{2}⁡x+3{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8a28f839-bb5d-5966-bf02-cc456e917b3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167418 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x={cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cosh}^{2}⁡x+3{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 3({cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int ({cosh}^{2}⁡x+{sinh}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95874" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{0}^{1}({cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f84738b9-eab0-5de7-ad81-984eef57a947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167419 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta ={cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sinh}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x={cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({cosh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+{sinh}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})+2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x+2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sinh}⁡1+{1}^{2}]-[\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0+{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡1+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186165734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}({cosh}^{2}⁡2x+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8bb7121c-56d4-5c48-ba76-846c281e39fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167421 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the following double-angle formula for cosine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the following double-angle formula for the hyperbolic cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta =2{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =2x$, we have\n\n$$\n{cosh}^{2}⁡2x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({cosh}^{2}⁡2x+x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+1)+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {1}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0+0-\\frac{1}{2}{0}^{2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡4+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167638 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167638 #edb/ref 1061 31435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167638 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "395f50bb-2ee7-5efe-bd0b-fd5e3bf3643e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167638 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167639 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167639 #edb/ref 1061 31436 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167639 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8c1d7230-7a0f-5272-ab0d-dd538abc9384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167639 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167640 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167640 #edb/ref 1061 31437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167640 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e8db643f-737e-55a3-9cb1-79d0ef4fba2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167640 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167641 #edb/ref 1061 31438 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167641 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "216b7d60-59dd-599b-b414-ed79dbefb05e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167641 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167735 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167735 #edb/ref 1061 34434 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167735 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bfc4d4ca-c5b7-55a0-9d68-e0e086fc3de2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167735 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168120 #edb/ref 1064 "We can compute integrals containing hyperbolic functions using the hyperbolic counterparts of the trigonometric double-angle formulas. We use Osborn's rule to convert a trigonometric identity to a corresponding hyperbolic identity. \n\nOsborn's rule states that to convert a trigonometric identity to a corresponding hyperbolic identity, we\n\n- replace every trigonometric function with its corresponding hyperbolic function, and\n\n- for any product of two trigonometric sines, change the sign of the corresponding product of hyperbolic sines.\n\n$\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sinh}{\\mathop{\\rm sinh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\cosh}{\\mathop{\\rm cosh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\tanh}{\\mathop{\\rm tanh}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n        \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFor example, let's consider the following integral:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sinh x \\cosh x \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that the corresponding trigonometric integral is\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle{\\int} \\sin x \\cos x \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\n  \n\nOne way of solving this trigonometric integral is to use the double-angle formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin 2x = 2\\sin x \\cos x\n$$\n\nApplying Osborn's rule, we get an equivalent hyperbolic identity:\n\n$$\n\\sinh 2x = 2\\sinh x \\cosh x\n$$\n\nRearranging the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\sinh {2x}= \\sinh x \\cosh x.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we can calculate our original integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168120 #edb/ref 1065 5558 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168120 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5aeb4951-903e-5815-85fe-2b3fdd1c992e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168120 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537225 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x+\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537225 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537225 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0126ad9c-e616-5191-8573-27abdacfd4c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537227 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+C" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537227 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537227 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0150030c-b66d-5338-9f85-6cd2ee3578f3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186537231 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡6x+C" #edb